        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ios): stop camera work when invoke is cancelled",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nFixes an issue where a timed-out iOS camera invoke could leave camera warm-up, an intentional delay, movie recording, or MP4 export running after the Gateway had already returned a timeout.\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\nCamera warm-up and delay now propagate cancellation, while recording and export use cancellation handlers to stop their AVFoundation operations. The existing session cleanup then runs as soon as the active operation returns.\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\nTimed-out or cancelled camera requests stop recording/exporting promptly instead of holding the camera or completing a stale operation in the background.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\n- `git diff --check` passed.\r\n- AI-assisted; one repository autoreview pass completed with no accepted findings.\r\n",
